What the screen gives us is not an equation in the narrow sense, but it is a formal structure: $\text{Is it fair that Wayne Rooney earns more than a care worker?}$ and the explicit two-way fork $\text{A. Yes, it is fair}
\qquad
\text{B. No, it is unfair}.$ That is already pedagogically significant. The lecture does not begin by telling us what fairness means. It begins by making us answer as though we already knew.

