The reported split is $\begin{aligned}
P(\text{fair}) &= 46\%,\\
P(\text{unfair}) &= 54\%.\end{aligned}$ Since the poll is binary, we may write the completion $P(\text{fair}) + P(\text{unfair}) = 100\%.$ Sandel’s remark that the room is pretty well divided is therefore not a throwaway comment. It is the reason to proceed. If the room had spoken with one voice, the lecture could have moved on. Instead, the near-even split turns the poll into a problem.

