p.src:
Her first point may be written as a conditional claim: $\text{equal chance in life}
\Longrightarrow
\text{stronger case that pay differences are fair}.$ Her second point shifts the measure of value: $\text{care worker services}
\Longrightarrow
\text{life-sustaining social value}.$ This is the lecture’s first major pivot. We move from consumer enjoyment and ticket prices to background justice and social importance. Lois does not deny that Rooney gives pleasure. She asks whether pleasure is the right standard by which to measure what a society should reward most highly.

