p.src:
The economist’s structure may be written as $\begin{aligned}
\text{many willing and able care workers}
&\Longrightarrow
\text{lower wage needed to elicit supply},\\
\text{scarce talent} + \text{high demand}
&\Longrightarrow
\text{higher wage}.\end{aligned}$ This is not a full model with curves and elasticities, and the lecture never pretends otherwise. But the logic is unmistakable: wages track the conjunction of supply conditions and demand conditions.

